p2-windows/W7 — page:admin/Users — native WinUI 3 UsersPage at web parity
================================================================================================
Web source : web/src/features/admin/pages/UsersPage.tsx  (the admin "Subjects" impersonation
             target picker; also reuses the already-ported web/src/features/admin/components/
             UserImpersonateButton.tsx)
Web route  : (unrouted)  — the web page ships unrouted (no routeRegistry entry); it is an
             importable-but-unrouted symbol reachable only from another bootstrap point.
Output     : apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/UsersPage/{UsersPage.cs,
             UsersPage.Model.cs, UsersPage.Source.cs, UsersPage.ViewModel.cs}
             (real in-repo path; the generated prompt's apps/windows/TeslaSync/Features/Admin/
              UsersPage.xaml path does NOT exist — the Windows app is TeslaSync.App with
              C#-markup feature-views, not XAML-per-page, and the platform string catalog lives at
              apps/windows/Strings/*.resw. This mirrors every prior W7 page in
              apps/parity/windows-ledger.json, e.g. windows-page-settings-ActiveSessionsPage.log.)

Shape of the parity unit (manifest id=page:admin/Users, requiredCount=10)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web page is a <PageContainer title subtitle> hosting a single <GlassPanel> (GlassPanel1) whose
body switches between five render branches, composed from two hooks:
  • useImpersonationStatus (GET /admin/impersonate)         -> open / inactive / active
  • useImpersonationCandidates (GET /admin/impersonate/candidates, enabled:!open)
  render: open ? openMode notice : candidates.isLoading ? Spinner : candidates.isError ?
          ErrorDisplay+retry : subjects.length===0 ? EmptyState : list of subjects, each row a
          <UserImpersonateButton subject disabled={active} />.
Manifest declares 4 data states (loading/empty/error/success), 1 panel (GlassPanel1) and 5 strings
(impersonation.users.{title,subtitle,openMode,emptyTitle,emptyMessage}). Honouring "no scope
narrowing / no stubs as final", the open-mode branch is also implemented in full (it carries the
impersonation.users.openMode manifest string) and the per-row impersonate action reuses the already
W7-ported native UserImpersonateButton surface (predecessor reuse; no second copy).

Native realisation (Fluent / WinUI 3, ADR-002/004/005/006/011)
--------------------------------------------------------------
- UsersPage : UserControl — mounts the shared PageContainer (parity port of web PageContainer) with
  PageContent = a Fluent TsGlassPanel (GlassPanel1) whose body switches between the loading notice
  (Spinner + caption), the open-mode notice (Warning glyph + HelperText), the failure surface
  (TsErrorDisplay + Retry), the empty surface (TsEmptyState title+message) and the subjects list
  (one Border row per subject: a monospace Code subject + a native UserImpersonateButton). Design
  tokens + a11y (AutomationProperties, Group peer, live-region feedback states) throughout. The
  per-row impersonate affordance is built by an injected factory; the parameterless (shell) page
  uses an inert IImpersonationSource (never invoked — the empty feed yields no rows), and the
  generated-client UsersPage.Create wires UserImpersonateButton.Create(api,engine,options,localizer).
- UsersPageViewModel : INotifyPropertyChanged — UI-thread-free state holder. Reads the status
  through IImpersonationSubjectsFeed (web useImpersonationStatus); when not open, reads the
  candidates (web useImpersonationCandidates, enabled:!open); projects UsersDisplay so the view is a
  thin renderer. LoadAsync/RefreshAsync; superseding CTS; no I/O in the view. A status transport
  fault resolves to Inactive (web parity: a status error leaves open/active false, so the candidates
  query still runs); a candidates failure drives the error surface.
- UsersProjection / UsersModel / UsersDisplay — pure projection (no WinUI types) resolving the
  five-branch matrix (open-mode / loading / error / empty / populated) in the web precedence order
  (ResolveState), the subjects = candidates.mode==='session'?candidates:[] rule, and the per-row
  disabled flag (web disabled={active}). ImpersonationCandidatesSnapshot.FromJson — tolerant parser
  ({mode,candidates} object, {data:[…]} envelope, bare array; explicit mode:'open' -> open snapshot).
- UsersPageRegistration — RouteName="Users", Slug="UsersPage", the two generated operation ids
  (get_api_v1_admin_impersonate, get_api_v1_admin_impersonate_candidates) + AUTH_MODE_OPEN sentinel,
  and every localized string keyed exactly as the web t(...) calls with the same English fallbacks.
- EmptyImpersonationSubjectsFeed — the no-backend default the parameterless (shell-registered) page
  hosts itself against (Inactive status + empty session candidates -> the friendly empty state, the
  web "single-subject install" case), mirroring the other W7 pages' Empty feeds.
  ImpersonationSubjectsClientFeed — the generated-OpenAPI-client adapter (ADR-004): the two GETs,
  mapping the 501 AUTH_MODE_OPEN to the open signal exactly as web useImpersonationStatus /
  useImpersonationCandidates do.
- Shell registration: apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/Shell/ShellWindow.xaml.cs registers
  PageFactory.Register("Users", () => new FeatureViews.Admin.UsersPage()). The web page is unrouted
  (no RouteTable entry), so this is a latent page-factory seam mirroring the web's wired-but-unrouted
  state — the same approach the shell already uses for the unrouted Diagnostic / RbacMatrix pages.

i18n note (R3/ADR-014)
----------------------
impersonation.users.{title,subtitle,openMode,emptyTitle,emptyMessage} (the five manifest strings) —
plus the ported supporting keys impersonation.users.{loading,error} and the shared common.retry —
are NOT catalog entries in either the web i18n source or the generated platform catalog
(apps/windows/Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw); the web resolves them as inline t(key, default)
fallbacks. The native surface resolves them the same way: keyed ILocalizer.GetString(key, <same
English default>) flowing through ShellLocalizer -> shell Localization (resw lookup -> English
fallback). Zero hardcoded literals; the auto-generated resw is left untouched (it is machine-
generated from web i18n; hand-editing would strand drift).

